Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"18bb1823-df86-194a-bd32-6a6c131df2a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"3adf15cd-cba4-834b-9d20-e06baca9065a"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d7bbb28f-b194-2740-ae38-7e8f65889de7"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"dd18a964-1fd8-3a43-827e-b295d493ed61"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1290ad3c-fd8d-9f45-944e-8c6c84f08e16"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"10ab6dad-a252-7a4f-995f-24123981685d"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"aad92018-3652-154b-83b3-195c12fe2ac2"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0fce5cb0-0815-9d43-a4c7-bdf0f066c012"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"86772952-3ad1-ca4b-95fc-c2f63ffe2eef"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"479ac2a7-5b76-c74f-aad0-1582a0078d46"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"69064a89-1293-3f43-b2a6-773f02c44c58"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"ab505818-1f3f-744f-860f-49721a2b0411"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cc322ebe-b24f-0549-ab1f-56accca7e56a"],

